KCFM‑v1.0 API Documentation

Kinetic‑Cryptographic Fluid Matrix — Cryptophysical Engine

Module overview

Module

Purpose

solver

Fluid dynamics (Navier–Stokes / Darcy)

tensorizer

State tensor fieldization + vectorization

entropy

Kinetic entropy computation

crypto

Key derivation + authenticated encryption

verification

Mass conservation + integrity checks

ledger

Cryptophysical state storage

1. solver module

1.1 Types

DomainConfigFields:

geometry: domain shape (e.g. "cylinder")

length: float

diameter: float

grid_resolution: {nx, ny, nz}

FluidPropertiesFields:

density: float ((\rho))

viscosity: float ((\mu))

BoundaryConditionsFields:

inlet_pressure(t): function or time series

outlet_pressure(t): function or time series

transient_events: list of events (e.g. motor hammer)

SolverStateFields:

pressure_field: 3D array

velocity_field: 3D vector field

turbulence_field: 3D array

time: float

1.2 Functions

initialize_solver(domain: DomainConfig, fluid: FluidProperties, bc: BoundaryConditions) -> SolverStateInitializes the CFD solver with geometry, fluid, and boundary conditions.

step_solver(state: SolverState, dt: float) -> SolverStateAdvances the solution by timestep dt, updating pressure, velocity, and turbulence fields.

compute_flow_rates(state: SolverState) -> {qin: float, qout: float}Computes inlet and outlet volumetric flow rates (Q_{\text{in}}, Q_{\text{out}}).

2. tensorizer module

2.1 Types

TensorStateFields:

tensor: 4D array [i,j,k,5] for ([p,u,v,w,\eta])

time: float

VectorStateFields:

vector: 1D array

time: float

2.2 Functions

build_tensor(state: SolverState) -> TensorStateMaps solver fields into tensor (T_{i,j,k}(t) = [p,u,v,w,\eta]).

flatten_tensor(tensor_state: TensorState) -> VectorStateFlattens tensor into high‑dimensional state vector (\mathbf{S}(t)).

3. entropy module

3.1 Types

EntropyStateFields:

kinetic_entropy: float

time: float

3.2 Functions

compute_kinetic_entropy(state: SolverState) -> EntropyStateComputes[ H_{\text{kinetic}} = \int |\nabla \mathbf{u}|^2 dV ]from the velocity field.

4. crypto module

4.1 Types

KeyStateFields:

key: bytes

time: float

CipherStateFields:

ciphertext: bytes

time: float

4.2 Functions

derive_key(entropy: EntropyState, vector: VectorState) -> KeyStateUses HKDF or similar:(K(t) = \text{HKDF}(H_{\text{kinetic}} \parallel \mathbf{S}(t))).

encrypt_state(vector: VectorState, key: KeyState) -> CipherStateEncrypts (\mathbf{S}(t)) with AES‑GCM‑SIV (and optional lattice layer).

5. verification module

5.1 Types

MassCheckFields:

delta_q: float

valid: bool

time: float

IntegrityCheckFields:

crc32: string

sha3: string

time: float

5.2 Functions

check_mass_conservation(flow: {qin: float, qout: float}) -> MassCheckComputes (\Delta Q = Q_{\text{in}} - Q_{\text{out}}) and validates (|\Delta Q| < 10^{-7}).

compute_integrity_hashes(cipher: CipherState) -> IntegrityCheckComputes CRC32 and SHA‑3 over ciphertext.

6. ledger module

6.1 Types

LedgerRecordFields:

time: float

ciphertext: bytes

delta_q: float

crc32: string

sha3: string

entropy: float

6.2 Functions

append_record(record: LedgerRecord) -> NoneAppends record to cryptophysical ledger (append‑only).

get_record(time: float) -> LedgerRecordRetrieves record closest to given time.

verify_record(record: LedgerRecord) -> boolRecomputes hashes and checks mass conservation to confirm integrity.

7. End‑to‑end pipeline helper

run_step(state: SolverState, dt: float) -> LedgerRecordPipeline:

step_solver

build_tensor

flatten_tensor

compute_kinetic_entropy

derive_key

encrypt_state

compute_flow_rates

check_mass_conservation

compute_integrity_hashes

append_record

Returns the LedgerRecord for that timestep.

